  "rm": {
    "rules": [
      {
        "args_contain": [
          ".env*"
        ],
        "decision": "deny",
        "reason": "Env files blocked"
      },
      {
        "fn": "all_paths_under_scratch",
        "decision": "allow",
        "reason": ""
      }
    ],
    "default": "deny",
    "reason": "rm is allowed ONLY under the scratch dir `.scratch/` at the repo root (the hook creates it and gitignores it for you). Put every throwaway there (temp scripts, scratch output, junk) and rm / rm -rf it freely — no prompt. Create files there with Write (it's in-tree and not under `.claude/`, so no edit prompt). Elsewhere in the tree, don't delete — move: `mv <path> .scratch/` retires the file with the same effect on the build and the tests, still shows up as a deletion in `git status` and the diff, and is one `mv` away from coming back when you were wrong. Say in your report what you moved and why, so the user can turn it into a real deletion."
  },
