  "claude": {
    "rules": [
      {
        "args_contain": [
          "--dangerously-skip-permissions"
        ],
        "decision": "deny",
        "reason": "`--dangerously-skip-permissions` disables the nested Claude's own permission gate, so that agent runs bash completely unchecked — an agent must not hand another agent a blank cheque. Drop the flag: a nested `claude -p` still runs under acl-hook (when enabled in the target project), which auto-approves safe commands and blocks dangerous ones. If the nested run stalls on prompts, set `ACL_HOOK_AUTONOMOUS=1` for it (every `ask` becomes a deny with a reason) or enable acl-hook in that project."
      },
      {
        "args_contain": [
          "-p",
          "--print"
        ],
        "decision": "allow",
        "reason": ""
      }
    ],
    "default": "deny",
    "reason": "Bare/interactive `claude` can't run under the agent at all — no TTY, so it just hangs; and subcommands like `mcp`/`config`/`update` change machine state. Run it headless instead: `claude -p \"<prompt>\"` (add `--permission-mode acceptEdits` for autonomous edits). For an interactive or config/update command, ask the user to run it in their own terminal."
  },
